## Put to the Point

The Swiss NGO section, which is affiliated to the Multilateral and Non-Governmental Organisations (NGO), is responsible for the SDC’s cooperation with internationally active Swiss NGOs. It shapes and manages the institutional partnerships with Swiss NGOs and is responsible for the awarding and support of core contributions.
To strengthen its team, the section is looking for a specialist in finance and administration.

- Entry date: 01.01.2027 or by agreement
- Type of employment: temporary
- Reference No: JRQ$540-20566
- Place of work: Eichenweg 5, 3052 Zollikofen

## You can make this contribution

- Responsibility for the management and quality assurance of the section’s finance and contract management in cooperation with the operational line;
- Advise the section on the drafting of contracts (budgets, payment plans and financial arrangements);
- control financial reports and accounts;
- monitor and monitor the progress and implementation of each phase of the project and programme (PCM);
- Manage and update the section’s information and data management tools (dashboard, QIikSense, etc.);
- Advise and support the section and department in budget planning and monitoring the existing processes.

## This makes them unique.

- professional qualification in economics, finance, accounting, administration, controlling and auditing or equivalent training;
- Significant interest in international cooperation and humanitarian aid, the activities of Swiss NGOs and the interface between civil society and federal administration;
- Good Excel knowledge and skill in dealing with computer and accounting programs (SAP, ESPRIT, Acta Nova, etc.);
- Good analytical skills, initiative, responsibility and resilience;
- Strong organisational and planning talent, communicative and team-capable personality;
- Excellent knowledge of two official languages as well as English.

## We offer this

- Working for Switzerland: We are committed to the Swiss success model and work for the benefit of the population.
- Living diversity: Thanks to equal opportunities, we develop our skills and bring in different perspectives.
- Healthy at work: We support and advise our employees in the field of physical and mental health.

On behalf of the Federal Council, the Federal Department of Foreign Affairs (FDA) coordinates and shapes Swiss foreign policy, safeguards the country’s interests and promotes Swiss values.

The Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) is Switzerland’s largest competence centre for international cooperation. The SDC implements Switzerland’s foreign policy in the areas of humanitarian aid, development cooperation and Eastern cooperation, in cooperation with other federal offices. It supports countries in combating poverty and tackling global challenges. For example, the SDC ensures that disadvantaged population groups have better access to education and health or that environmental problems are solved. The SDC focuses on fragile and conflict-affected countries.

## Additional information

Application deadline: 28.10.2026

